UNITED STATES MISSION TO THE UNITED NATIONS
Office of Press and Public Diplomacy
FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE
Press Release: Ambassador Mike Waltz Welcomes Ellie Cohanim to the U.S. Mission to the United Nations
New York – This week, U.S. Representative to the United Nations Ambassador Mike Waltz welcomed Ellie Cohanim as Senior Policy Advisor at the U.S. Mission to the United Nations.
A lifelong New Yorker who was born in Tehran, her family fled Iran in 1979 after the Islamic Revolution and the escalating persecution of Iran’s Jewish community. Her family’s story has shaped her lifelong commitment to freedom, human dignity, and American leadership.
“Ellie’s story is the American story,” said Ambassador Waltz. “Her family fled persecution in Iran, built a life in New York, and she has spent her career looking for ways to serve America, fighting for freedom, standing with the persecuted, and calling out antisemitism wherever it hides. That is exactly the kind of conviction and courage we need at the United Nations.”
Cohanim previously served as U.S. Deputy Special Envoy to Monitor and Combat Antisemitism at the Department of State during President Donald J. Trump’s first administration. As the Department’s first Iranian-born Envoy, she led U.S. diplomatic efforts to combat antisemitism across the Near East and Western Hemisphere and helped forge groundbreaking partnerships with Arab nations as part of the Abraham Accords’ “Warm Peace” team.
Before joining USUN, Cohanim was a Senior Fellow at Independent Women’s Forum and served on the Trump-Vance Presidential Transition’s National Security/State Department Team. She has written and spoken extensively on Iran, the Middle East, religious freedom, global antisemitism, and America First foreign policy.
Cohanim is fluent in Farsi and Hebrew and is familiar with Arabic.
