New York – U.S. Representative for UN Management and Reform Ambassador Jeff Bartos shared the historic scope of U.S.-led reforms to the UN as part of the Trump Administration’s America First foreign policy in an interview with Fox News.
Speaking to the network, Ambassador Bartos declared that “UN reform is no longer an oxymoron,” highlighting a landmark $570 million reduction in the global body’s budget. Less than a year into his tenure, Bartos points to these historic cuts as evidence that the Trump Administration is successfully reshaping a bloated and inefficient system detached from its core mission.
As Bartos shared with the network, reforming the UN was considered impossible until President Trump came along. “Under the President’s vision and leadership, the United States is driving culture change at the UN. Being efficient, being respectful of every dollar, thinking about the taxpayers who fund all this.”
